            <ArticleTitle>Conjugatable and Bioreduction Cleavable Linker for the 5'-Functionalization of Oligonucleotides.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1796-1802</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.joc.6b02527</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An efficient conjugatable and bioreduction cleavable linker was designed and synthesized for the 5'-terminal ends of oligonucleotides. A phosphoramidite reagent bearing this linker was successfully applied to solid phase synthesis and incorporated at the 5'-terminal ends of oligonucleotides. The controlled pore glass (CPG)-supported oligonucleotides were subsequently conjugated to a diverse range of functional molecules using a CuAAC reaction. The synthesized oligonucleotide conjugates were then cleaved using a nitroreductase/NADH bioreduction system to release the naked oligonucleotides.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
